---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base
  title="About PrenupAnswers — Who Writes This & How We're Funded"
  description="Meet Francisco Gomes — pastor, marital counselor, and the writer behind PrenupAnswers. Who writes this site, how it makes money, and what it will never do."
>
  <section class="article-head">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="crumbs"><a href="/">Home</a> / About</p>
      <h1>About PrenupAnswers</h1>
      <p class="meta">Independent. Educational. Not a law firm — and never will be.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <div class="prose">
    <div class="author-intro">
      <figure class="author-photo">
        <img
          src="/images/francisco-gomes.jpg"
          alt="Francisco Gomes and his wife"
          width="1200"
          height="1600"
          fetchpriority="high"
        />
        <figcaption>Francisco and his wife</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Who writes this</p>
        <h2 style="margin-top:.2rem;">Francisco Gomes</h2>
        <p class="author-role">Pastor · Marital counselor · Writer · Law student</p>
        <p style="color:var(--muted);">
          Francisco is a pastor and marital counselor. Most of his working life has been spent in the hardest room
          in any marriage: the money conversation — the one where one partner is afraid to say a number, the other
          is afraid to ask, and both are afraid that wanting a prenup means admitting the marriage might fail.
        </p>
        <p style="color:var(--muted);">
          PrenupAnswers grew out of those conversations. Too many couples reach the wedding with the money talk
          still undone — armed with forum myths, law-firm sales pitches, and wedding blogs that pretend these
          questions don't exist. This site is the third thing: plain-English, sourced answers you can read in one
          sitting and act on today.
        </p>
        <p style="color:var(--muted);">
          <strong>Francisco is also a law student</strong> — and that is exactly why this site is careful about its
          boundaries. He is not a lawyer, this is not a law firm, and nothing here is legal advice. When your
          situation needs an attorney — a business, a trust, a prior marriage with children — the answer is a
          licensed lawyer in your state, full stop.
        </p>
        <p style="color:var(--muted);">
          PrenupAnswers is written from Brazil for readers across the United States. Every state's rules are
          researched from primary sources — state statutes, court self-help pages, published pricing — and checked
          against the current year before anything gets published.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h2>How we're funded</h2>
    <p>
      Two ways, and that's it: affiliate partnerships and display advertising. If you click a link to an online prenup
      service and buy something, we may earn a commission at no extra cost to you. See the full
      <a href="/disclosure/">affiliate disclosure</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Commission never decides what we recommend.</strong> If a cheaper path is the right path for your
      situation, that's what the article says — even when it earns us nothing.
    </p>

    <h2>What we will never do</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Sell legal services or draft agreements</li>
      <li>Pretend to be lawyers or offer legal advice</li>
      <li>Hide affiliate links behind vague language</li>
      <li>Publish cost figures we can't source</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>When you actually need a lawyer</h2>
    <p>
      Online services are fine for straightforward situations. But if one partner owns a business, there's a
      family-trust, complex stock comp, real estate across states, or a prior marriage with children involved — talk
      to a licensed family-law attorney in your state. A few hundred dollars of advice up front is cheap insurance
      for a document that governs your finances for life.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions, corrections, or a source we missed? Email <strong>hello@prenupanswers.com</strong>. We read every
      message — corrections get fixed within 48 hours.
    </p>
  </div>

  <style>
    .author-intro {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: 200px 1fr;
      gap: 1.5rem;
      align-items: start;
      margin-bottom: 1rem;
    }
    .author-photo { margin: 0; }
    .author-photo img {
      width: 100%;
      border-radius: 14px;
      border: 1px solid var(--line);
      box-shadow: 0 8px 24px rgba(8, 26, 46, .12);
    }
    .author-photo figcaption {
      font-size: .78rem;
      color: var(--muted);
      text-align: center;
      margin-top: .5rem;
      font-style: italic;
    }
    .author-role {
      font-size: .85rem;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      letter-spacing: .1em;
      color: var(--gold-dark);
      font-weight: 800;
      margin-top: -.4rem;
    }
    @media (max-width: 700px) {
      .author-intro { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
      .author-photo { max-width: 240px; margin: 0 auto; }
    }
  </style>
</Base>
